# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using pnpm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Lock file `pnpm-lock.yaml` updated with 411 new packages

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified:** `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, following the recommended placement from the official documentation

## Implementation Details

The project uses:
- **Framework:** Next.js 16.2.6 with App Router
- **Package Manager:** pnpm
- **Integration Type:** Next.js-specific integration using `@vercel/speed-insights/next`

The SpeedInsights component was placed just before the closing `</body>` tag, after the main application content and Providers wrapper. This placement ensures:
- The component is loaded on all pages
- Minimal impact on initial page load
- Proper tracking of Core Web Vitals across the application

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build verified successfully with `pnpm build`
- Compilation completed without errors
- All 13 routes generated successfully
- TypeScript checks passed

✅ Linting verified for modified file
- No linting errors introduced in `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Pre-existing linting issues in other files were not affected

✅ Lock files properly updated
- `pnpm-lock.yaml` includes all new dependencies

## Next Steps

To start seeing Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights → Enable)
3. Wait for user visits to collect Core Web Vitals data
4. View metrics in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes

- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation exactly as specified
- No breaking changes were introduced to existing functionality
- The SpeedInsights component will automatically collect and report performance metrics when deployed on Vercel
- Pre-existing linting errors in chart components were identified but not addressed as they are unrelated to this implementation
